# Byteman rule for memtable_heap_space-tryAllocate-limit, §9d "Bypass volume".
#
# Traces every call to MemtableAllocator$SubAllocator.allocated(long). At
# cassandra-5.0.9 that method is private and has one caller: the escape hatch in
# allocate() (MemtableAllocator.java:180-183), where a write whose OpOrder group a
# flush has marked blocking (ColumnFamilyStore.java:1238) is forced past the limit
# instead of waiting. Every flush marks its barrier blocking, so the rule counts
# force-throughs from any flush, not only scenario C's.
#
# One line per forced allocation:
#
#   forced=<bytes> limit=<pool limit in bytes> ms=<epoch millis> thread=<name>
#
# The bypass volume is the sum of `forced`. `limit` names the pool: the on-heap
# pool's limit is memtable_heap_space in bytes.
#
# Output file: the system property stage4.byteman.out, or else escape-hatch.txt
# in the JVM's working directory.

RULE escape hatch forces an allocation past the limit
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.utils.memory.MemtableAllocator$SubAllocator
METHOD allocated(long)
AT ENTRY
IF true
DO traceOpen("escapeHatch", java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.byteman.out", "escape-hatch.txt"));
   traceln("escapeHatch", "forced=" + $1 + " limit=" + $0.parent.limit + " ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis() + " thread=" + java.lang.Thread.currentThread().getName())
ENDRULE
